SUMMARY:ABCD Reads "Go Gentle" by Maria Semple
DESCRIPTION:A Book Club\, Downtown (ABCD)\nABCD Reads "[Go Gentle](https:/
 /tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/record/S234C4718443)" by Maria Semple.\n\n([RESU
 LTS](https://opavote.com/results/6419002495860736) of the poll for this ev
 ent.)\n\n**:: ABOUT THE BOOK ::**\n"Adora Hazzard has it all figured out. 
 A Stoic philosopher and divorcée\, she lives a contented life on New York
  City’s Upper West Side. Having discovered that the secret to happiness 
 is to desire only what you have\, she’s applied this insight to blissful
  effect: relishing her teenage daughter\, the freedom of being solo\, and 
 her job as a moral tutor for the twin boys of an old-money family. She’s
  even assembled a “coven”—like-minded women who live on the same flo
 or in the legendary Ansonia—and is making active efforts to grow its mem
 bership. Adora’s carefully curated life is humming along brilliantly unt
 il a chance meeting with a handsome stranger." (from [Goodreads](https://w
 ww.goodreads.com/book/show/239152335-go-gentle))\n\n"ATV comedy writer tur
 ned popularizer of Stoic philosophy falls in love\, is swept into an inter
 national art incident\, and deals with buried trauma. For starters.\nA wil
 d mess of a plot\, but a fun wild mess\, punctuated by Semple’s signatur
 e witty observations and punchlines." (from [Kirkus Reviews](https://www.k
 irkusreviews.com/book-reviews/maria-semple/go-gentle/))\n\n**:: ABOUT THE 
 EVENT ::**\nYou are welcome to arrive 30 minutes before the event and stay
  30 minutes or longer afterward to connect with other attendees outside th
 e book talk.\n\nPlease ensure you have read the book before attending (tho
 ugh finishing any book is not a barrier to participating\, as long as you 
 don't mind spoilers).\n\nFirst-time attendees can join for free. If the ev
 ent is full\, we maintain an unofficial waitlist. Please send [Michael](ht
 tps://www.meetup.com/members/55295192/) a direct message for more informat
 ion\, in either case.\n\nWe request a $3 contribution from regular attende
 es to help cover our monthly meetup costs.\n\n**:: ABOUT OUR NEXT BOOK ::*
 *\nAt the end of each event\, we will ask for nominees for our next book. 
 If you have a good one in mind\, please ensure it is between 200-400 pages
  long\, available from the Toronto Public Library\, and counts as contempo
 rary literary fiction (though these are not hard and fast rules). When eno
 ugh nominees are collected\, Michael will send the members a direct messag
 e with a link where you can vote.
